* All analysed issue types demonstrate high CSAT scores. However, both AHT and TRT require improvement across all three issue types.
* Consistently across both quarters, the most frequently reported issue was scratches or dents on vehicles, representing over 50% of the reported cases.
* The Q4 data reveals a significant improvement in CSAT for all three issue types, as well as improvements in AHT and TRT specifically for issues related to vehicle scratches or dents and dirty or smelly vehicles.
* While less frequent, the issue of odd noises experienced a notable increase in TRT during Q4. This require an investigation to determine the underlying cause of the extended resolution time.
* A discrepancy exists in the Q4 data, where the TRT for issues involving dirty or smelly vehicles is lower than the AHT. This anomaly requires further clarification and analysis.

