+*_Key findings:_*+

* *Case Volume:* Latvia, Germany, and Estonia consistently show the highest number of reported cases in both Q3 and Q4. Portugal was launched 11.11.2024, which explains the lack of data for Q3. 
* *CSAT:* Most countries maintain high CSAT scores (above 90%) in both quarters, indicating general customer satisfaction. However, Poland's CSAT dropped significantly from Q3 (91%) to Q4 (72%). Latvia showed the highest CSAT in Q4 at 99%.
* *AHT:* Poland has notably high AHT values in both quarters, which are much higher than other countries. It should be investigated, as issues with vehicle condition is part of 3P partner responsibility and Bolt’s CS should not be involved.  Estonia shows a decrease in AHT from Q3 to Q4, suggesting improved handling efficiency. Portugal also has high AHT in Q4, but this is based on a very small number of cases. 
* *TRT:* Lithuania has a very high TRT in Q3, which significantly decreases in Q4 below of AHT level. At the same time the Czech Republic’s TRT increased substantially from Q3 to Q4. Poland’s TRT is low in both quarters, because the issues with vehicle condition should be handled by 3P partner.  Portugal has a high TRT in Q4, but is based on limited data.

