I’ve just received a few comments from Jelena, you can find them below. I have included most of them in the draft, but I will need your help to draft them in the right way ([Service Agreement draft|https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nEjxEkKMAgFxSuXysYRqjUEsHUdUsmgXkeuiadDc5FU/edit?tab=t.0]).



# {color:#0747a6}_Minimum Workload_{color}

{color:#0747a6}_Since the contract implies part-time employment, I would like to establish a minimum workload of at least 10 full working days per month._ {color}

{color:#0747a6}_This will allow me to plan my workload effectively and balance my time between projects._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_Additionally, if Bolt decides to terminate my services, it would be reasonable to include a minimum notice period of two weeks, allowing me to adjust accordingly and organize my work process._{color}



# {color:#0747a6}_Creative Freedom and Conceptual Ideas_{color}

{color:#0747a6}_Since the contract is for part-time engagement, it naturally leaves room for professional development and the opportunity to take on additional projects. It is important for me to understand that I am free to work on other tasks, including projects related to creative concepts._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_At times, my ideas and research might intersect with topics related to mobility or everyday situations, but I may not always be aware of all of Bolt’s projects. Hypothetically, there is a possibility of touching upon a related subject._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_Of course, I fully respect Bolt’s confidentiality policy, image, and reputation, and I will not publish anything directly related to the company’s projects, especially tender proposal details._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_If Bolt ever has any concerns, I am open to discussing them and, if necessary, providing materials for review or considering potential adjustments._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_At the same time, as I am not a full-time Bolt employee, I will need to seek other projects for my professional growth._{color}



# {color:#0747a6}_Intellectual Property and Rights to Work_{color}

{color:#0747a6}_The contract states that all rights to the work I create will fully belong to Bolt, including those that may have been created before my collaboration with the company._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_This raises questions, as I have worked on various concepts and designs before signing the contract._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_I am open to discussing which specific works Bolt is interested in and which the company wants to retain rights to. However, it is important for me to maintain the freedom to use my ideas and previous developments, provided they are not directly related to tasks performed for Bolt._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_That said, I would be more than happy to develop similar concepts within the scope of our collaboration._{color}



# {color:#0747a6}_Contract Review in 3 Months_{color}

{color:#0747a6}_As we initially discussed, I would like to establish that we will review the terms of our collaboration in three months._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_If our cooperation proves successful for both sides, I would be happy to consider transitioning into a full-time position at Bolt, focusing exclusively on developing materials and projects for the company._{color}



# {color:#0747a6}_Freelance Format and Taxation Challenges_{color}

{color:#0747a6}_In Portugal, as a freelancer, I am required to manage my own taxes through the Recibo Verde system, which has many complexities._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_I have examples of colleagues who have faced penalties due to reporting inaccuracies. This creates certain risks and uncertainty, and I do not wish to consider this format of cooperation in the long term._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_This is why it is important for me to understand the prospects of a full-time position in the future._{color}



# {color:#0747a6}_Approval of Work Stages and Payment_{color}

{color:#0747a6}_The contract states that the company can refuse payment if it deems the work incompetent._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_However, in practice, all tasks are reviewed and approved by colleagues, and intermediate stages are validated by responsible team members._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_Therefore, if a stage of work was approved during the process, it means that it meets the company’s established standards and falls within the competence of the approving persons._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_This will help avoid situations where previously approved work is later deemed unsatisfactory._{color}

{color:#0747a6}_Of course, I always strive to deliver my work at the highest possible level, and I am open to feedback and suggestions from colleagues, particularly those related to corporate branding and tender processes._{color}

